build: link nghttp2 and OpenSSL where their headers are included

microtel_sdk includes <nghttp2/nghttp2.h> and <openssl/ssl.h> through
transport/http2_transport.hpp but linked neither, so it built only where
both are in the host's /usr/include.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/microtel-org/microtel/issues/473]

diff --git a/src/sdk/CMakeLists.txt b/src/sdk/CMakeLists.txt
index 39d9a16..d64ea01 100644
--- a/src/sdk/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/sdk/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -59,7 +59,13 @@ target_link_libraries(microtel_sdk
             microtel_http_wire
             microtel_grpc_wire
             microtel_custom_wire
-            microtel_encoder)
+            microtel_encoder
+            # sdk_builder.cpp includes transport/http2_transport.hpp, which
+            # includes <nghttp2/nghttp2.h> and <openssl/ssl.h>.
+            # microtel_transport links both PRIVATE, so their include paths
+            # do not reach this target (#473).
+            OpenSSL::SSL
+            PkgConfig::NGHTTP2)
 
 target_include_directories(microtel_sdk
     PRIVATE ${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/src)
